1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:21,155
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June twenty-ninth. Okinawa's rainy season ends, the thirty-two teams for the World Cup knockout round are decided with Japan set to face Brazil, and a train derails at Kyoto Station with no injuries. Let's listen.

2
00:00:21,756 --> 00:00:24,515
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:25,216 --> 00:00:28,696
[News] 沖縄で梅雨が明けました。

4
00:00:29,396 --> 00:00:37,795
[News] 気象庁は29日、沖縄地方が梅雨明けしたとみられると発表しました。

5
00:00:38,496 --> 00:00:46,896
[News] 今年の梅雨明けは、平年より8日遅く、去年より22日遅いです。

6
00:00:47,595 --> 00:00:56,307
[News] これから沖縄では、太平洋高気圧に覆われて、暑い夏が続きそうです。

7
00:00:57,008 --> 00:01:08,120
[News] 次のニュースです。サッカーのワールドカップで、決勝トーナメントに進む32チームが出そろいました。

8
00:01:08,819 --> 00:01:16,091
[News] グループステージが終わり、決勝トーナメントの組み合わせが決まりました。

9
00:01:16,792 --> 00:01:22,983
[News] 日本代表は、次の試合でブラジルと対戦します。

10
00:01:23,683 --> 00:01:29,924
[News] 森保監督は「勝って歴史を変えたい」と話しました。

11
00:01:30,623 --> 00:01:37,680
[News] 最後のニュースです。京都駅で電車が脱線しました。

12
00:01:38,379 --> 00:01:46,731
[News] 29日の朝、近鉄京都線の電車が京都駅の中で脱線しました。

13
00:01:47,432 --> 00:01:53,912
[News] この事故で、乗客や乗務員にけが人はいませんでした。

14
00:01:54,611 --> 00:02:01,524
[News] 近鉄は原因を調べて、早く復旧したいと話しています。

15
00:02:02,224 --> 00:02:03,855
[Host] Let's break it down.

16
00:02:04,456 --> 00:02:14,056
[Slow] 気象庁は29日、沖縄地方が梅雨明けしたとみられると発表しました。

17
00:02:14,855 --> 00:02:21,575
[Host] On the twenty-ninth, the weather agency announced that Okinawa appears to have come out of the rainy season.

18
00:02:22,175 --> 00:02:24,671
[Vocab] 梅雨明け

19
00:02:25,072 --> 00:02:33,759
[Host] The end of the rainy season. Japan has a wet season in early summer, and this word marks the day it finishes and real summer begins.

20
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:44,295
[Slow] これから沖縄では、太平洋高気圧に覆われて、暑い夏が続きそうです。

21
00:02:45,096 --> 00:02:53,352
[Host] From now on, Okinawa will be covered by the Pacific high-pressure system, and a hot summer looks set to continue.

22
00:02:53,951 --> 00:02:56,592
[Vocab] 高気圧

23
00:02:56,991 --> 00:03:04,599
[Host] High-pressure system. In weather forecasts, this is the area that usually brings clear, sunny skies.

24
00:03:05,199 --> 00:03:10,743
[Slow] 決勝トーナメントの組み合わせが決まりました。

25
00:03:11,544 --> 00:03:14,951
[Host] The matchups for the knockout round have been decided.

26
00:03:15,551 --> 00:03:18,168
[Vocab] 組み合わせ

27
00:03:18,568 --> 00:03:25,743
[Host] A pairing or matchup. It comes from the verb meaning to combine, so it's which team is paired against which.

28
00:03:26,343 --> 00:03:33,400
[Slow] 日本代表は、次の試合でブラジルと対戦します。

29
00:03:34,199 --> 00:03:38,448
[Host] The Japan national team will play against Brazil in their next match.

30
00:03:39,048 --> 00:03:41,328
[Vocab] 対戦

31
00:03:41,728 --> 00:03:48,135
[Host] To face off or compete against. You'll hear it constantly in sports for one side playing another.

32
00:03:48,735 --> 00:03:55,912
[Slow] 近鉄京都線の電車が京都駅の中で脱線しました。

33
00:03:56,711 --> 00:04:01,199
[Host] A Kintetsu Kyoto Line train derailed inside Kyoto Station.

34
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:04,032
[Vocab] 脱線

35
00:04:04,431 --> 00:04:12,256
[Host] Derailment, when a train comes off the rails. The first character means to slip off, the second means track.

36
00:04:12,855 --> 00:04:20,271
[Slow] この事故で、乗客や乗務員にけが人はいませんでした。

37
00:04:21,072 --> 00:04:26,711
[Host] In this accident, there were no injured people among the passengers or crew.

38
00:04:27,312 --> 00:04:29,567
[Vocab] けが人

39
00:04:29,968 --> 00:04:38,632
[Host] An injured person. It joins the word for injury with the character for person, and it's a word you hear in almost every accident report.

40
00:04:39,232 --> 00:04:42,232
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

41
